  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation strengthens the main set of supported dataset-specific associations. For H5, the original hypothesis that KEAP1 loss is associated with stronger NFE2L2 dependency remains rejected. The independent validation R13, registered under direction -1, is signed negative, estimate -0.791 with an independent interval entirely negative, [-0.821, -0.761]. Because estimates are already signed to the registered direction, this negative result indicates that the raw KEAP1-loss minus KEAP1-intact difference in dependency_NFE2L2 is positive: KEAP1-loss cells have higher, less negative dependency_NFE2L2 scores. Thus validation confirms the direction reversal captured by H19 rather than the original H5 direction. For H9, independent validation R39 strongly supports the MSI-high association: signed estimate +0.8215 with an independent interval entirely positive, [0.766, 0.877], at the validation alpha threshold. This is consistent with discovery R8, signed estimate +0.7899. The raw interpretation is that MSI-high cells have dependency_WRN scores about 0.82 units lower, i.e. much stronger WRN dependency. The magnitude is more than three WRN outcome SDs and far exceeds a 10% relative-difference threshold when interpreted cautiously, although relative ratios are awkward because dependency scores are centered near zero. H9 is therefore accepted as an independently validated dataset-level association and closed as a primary claim. For H20, independent validation R40 supports the TP53-intact KEAP1 context: signed estimate +0.7948 with independent interval [0.764, 0.826], consistent with discovery R24. This confirms that the KEAP1-loss association with weaker NFE2L2 dependency is large in TP53-intact cells, while prior discovery H26 indicates a similar large effect in TP53-loss cells, though H26 itself has not been independently validated. Overall supported associations now include: SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, validated by R7/R26; MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, validated by R8/R39; and KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, validated in the reversed H19 and in the TP53-intact conditional H20. The accepted set also includes large conditional/context claims: SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency in adenocarcinoma and ARID1A-intact cells; MSI-high WRN dependency in adenocarcinoma and adherent culture; and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency in TP53-loss cells. Negative and robustness findings remain meaningful: original H5 is rejected; marker D and marker F constructed controls are near null for SMARCA2, WRN, and NFE2L2; marker D/F interactions are near null; the WRN subtype interaction is null; ARID1A loss in SMARCA4-intact cells is null for SMARCA2; and BRCA2 loss in MSI-negative cells is null for WRN. The most informative next work is to complete the marker-E control suite, test media-serum and other culture/technical contexts, and continue to probe remaining driver and MYC-associated hypotheses without claiming causality or generalizability. All conclusions remain associations within this supplied dataset, not causal or external-validity claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current validated primary dataset associations: H7 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H9 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; H19 reversed KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. H20 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency in TP53-intact cells is now independently validated. H26 KEAP1/NFE2L2 in TP53-loss remains accepted from discovery but not validated. Accepted context/conditional claims: H21 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 in adenocarcinoma, H22 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 among ARID1A-intact, H23 MSI/WRN in adenocarcinoma, H55 MSI/WRN in adherent culture. Negative/robustness findings: H5 rejected; marker D and marker F main effects near null; marker D/F interactions near null; WRN lineage interaction null; ARID1A loss among SMARCA4-intact null; BRCA2 loss among MSI-negative null. Unresolved but not supported: EGFR amplification overall H3 is near-null/near threshold; KRAS/BRAF/ERBB2 driver hypotheses and many MYC/MDM2/STAT3/DHX9/USP7/RPL11/POLR2A/RIT1/TMED10/KIF18A comparisons remain unresolved. Next planned analyses: marker-E main controls already registered and marker-E interactions newly proposed; media-serum 5% main effects for accepted associations newly proposed; culture_type interaction for KEAP1/NFE2L2 newly proposed; later test remaining media_serum_pct interactions and unresolved driver hypotheses. Keep all conclusions dataset-specific."
