  "narrative": "This wave mostly strengthens the robustness picture while producing one new biologically interesting MDM2 result and one unexpected opposite KRAS result. H99 is the strongest new finding: among TP53-intact cells, CDKN2A loss is associated with substantially stronger MDM2 dependency. The signed estimate is +0.1185 with CI [0.0793, 0.1577], meaning the raw CDKN2A-loss minus intact difference is approximately -0.119, i.e. more negative dependency. Relative to the MDM2 dependency mean magnitude (~0.269), even the lower bound is about a 29% difference, well above the 10% clinical-significance threshold. I accept H99 and request independent validation because it is a new, precise, mechanistically plausible association not yet externally checked in this run. H107 confirms that the KEAP1/NFE2L2 association is not an artifact of STK11 co-loss: among STK11-intact cells, KEAP1 loss still shows a very large positive signed effect (+0.801, CI [0.779, 0.823]) for weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Given the already accepted and validated KEAP1/NFE2L2 main and TP53-stratified claims, I accept and close this as a context-specific robustness association. H100 remains unresolved because the MTAP-loss point effect is small (~+0.024 signed; raw stronger by 0.024, ~9% of MDM2 mean magnitude), but the upper CI bound allows a clinically meaningful effect. H101 rejects the registered prediction that NF1 loss in KRAS-wild-type cells predicts stronger KRAS dependency; the interval is entirely negative for the signed hypothesis direction, implying raw exposed-minus-comparator is positive/less negative, i.e. weaker KRAS dependency. That opposite effect is statistically clear and roughly 16% of the KRAS mean magnitude at the point estimate, so I reject the original claim and register a reversed post-hoc claim linked to H101 for future investigation. H102 is rejected because ERBB2 amplification in KRAS-wild-type cells shows a near-null interval whose positive tail is below the 10% threshold for dependency_ERBB2. The MYC high-expression restrictions mostly reject the stronger-dependency hypotheses: DHX9, POLR2A, and RPL11 effects are near zero and their positive tails are below 10% of the respective outcome means. USP7 is left unresolved/deferred because the interval is wide enough to include clinically meaningful effects in either direction, despite the point estimate being near zero. The screen-quality interactions H108-H110 do not support important moderation; their signed estimates are small and their intervals, evaluated relative to the very large main effects they moderate, do not indicate a meaningful interaction. They therefore support stability of the accepted SMARCA4/SMARCA2, MSI/WRN, and KEAP1/NFE2L2 associations. I also close the already accepted context claims H21 and H22 because they are sufficiently characterized as dataset-specific context associations. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset and not causal or externally generalizable effects.",
  "research_notes": "Core independently validated dataset associations: H7/H19/H20/H26 plus context claims show (1) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; (2) MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; (3) KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency, robust across TP53 strata and library/STK11 checks. New accepted discovery association: H99 CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact cells -> stronger MDM2 dependency; signed estimate +0.1185 [0.0793,0.1577], raw approx -0.119, CI excludes 0 and is clinically large; independent validation requested for H99. Accepted robustness/context: H107 KEAP1 loss among STK11-intact cells -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency, signed +0.801 [0.779,0.823]; closed because KEAP1/NFE2L2 signal is already extensively validated. Closed context claims H21 and H22 remain accepted: SMARCA4/SMARCA2 effect in adenocarcinoma and ARID1A-intact contexts. Negative/null this wave: H102 ERBB2 amp among KRAS-wild-type rejected; H103/H105/H106 MYC amplified high-expression MYC effects rejected for DHX9/POLR2A/RPL11 as intervals do not support >=10% stronger dependency; H108/H109/H110 screen_roc_auc interactions rejected as small relative to accepted main effects. Reversed finding: H101 original NF1-loss-in-KRAS-wildtype stronger KRAS dependency prediction rejected; observed opposite direction (NF1 loss associated with weaker KRAS dependency) with signed estimate -0.0387 [-0.0712,-0.0062]; registered new post-hoc reversed claim linked to H101 for possible future testing. Unresolved/deferred: H100 MTAP loss among TP53-intact MDM2 remains unresolved because CI upper bound crosses clinically meaningful threshold though point is small; H104 USP7 MYC amplified high-expression remains unresolved/deferred due wide interval. Prior negatives/near-nulls still stand: constructed marker D/E/F, library/batch/media context main-effect checks where near null, BRCA2 among MSI-negative, growth-rate interactions, mutation-burden MSI interaction invalid due structural overlap. Next priorities: assess validation for H99; follow up reversed NF1/KRAS claim if resources allow; complete registered media-serum, Cas9-activity, ploidy, mutation-burden, and remaining interaction hypotheses for accepted associations; test remaining unresolved main-effect hypotheses only if they are biologically specific and likely to be precise. All statements remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
