  "narrative": "This appraise wave mostly tests robustness and specificity of previously accepted associations, and the central accepted associations remain strong. For PTEN loss and stronger STAT3 dependency, the effect is robust in three contexts: TP53-intact cells (H128, signed +0.287 [0.227,0.347]), PIK3CA-wild-type cells (H132, signed +0.267 [0.210,0.323]), and adenocarcinoma cells (H136, signed +0.268 [0.206,0.330]). The lower bounds are all many times the 10% absolute-mean benchmark for dependency_STAT3 (~0.282), so these are strong dataset-specific associations rather than fragile context artifacts. For TP53 loss and weaker USP7 dependency, the effect is robust in the dominant Avana library (H127, signed +0.405 [0.330,0.479]) and in MTAP-intact cells (H130, signed +0.421 [0.343,0.498]), far above the 10% benchmark for dependency_USP7 (~0.175). For CDKN2A loss and stronger MDM2 dependency, the association remains strong in PTEN-intact cells (H139, signed +0.116 [0.078,0.153]), again above the 10% benchmark for dependency_MDM2 (~0.269). These context acceptances should be interpreted as robustness checks within the supplied dataset, not as mechanistic causality claims.\n\nThe direct interaction tests are less decisive. The USP7 TP53-loss effect does not show evidence of moderation by CDKN2A loss (H131, signed -0.004 [-0.177,0.170]); the interval is wide and allows clinically meaningful interaction in either direction, so this remains unresolved rather than rejected. The CDKN2A/MDM2 lineage interaction is also near null and imprecise (H126, signed -0.010 [-0.088,0.068]); the accepted CDKN2A/MDM2 association does not require lineage-specific moderation, so I defer further follow-up. SMAD4 loss and STAT3 dependency is near null with wide uncertainty (H117, signed +0.011 [-0.026,0.047]); the upper bound allows a meaningful effect, but the evidence is not supportive, so it is deferred.\n\nH135 is rejected as originally registered: TP53 loss was not associated with stronger DHX9 dependency. The signed interval is entirely negative, meaning the raw contrast is positive (TP53 loss associated with weaker DHX9 dependency), but the raw magnitude interval is small (~0.001 to 0.039) and only the upper portion crosses the 10% benchmark for dependency_DHX9. I therefore do not accept the opposite direction, but I register it as a new exploratory reversal linked to H135 because the raw interval is on one side of zero. H146 and H147 are inconclusive: RB1 loss among faster-growing cells and BRCA2 loss for POLR2A have intervals that include both null and potentially meaningful effects, but point estimates are small; I defer them. Overall, the most important pending action is independent validation of the main PTEN/STAT3 association (H116), which remains unvalidated despite strong context support.",
