  "narrative": "No assessments are due. I register twelve targeted mean_difference tests that localize already accepted dataset-specific dependency axes into biologically distinct contexts rather than broad near-null scanning. Direction conventions follow earlier claims: direction -1 represents stronger dependency and direction +1 represents weaker dependency, because dependency scores are more negative when stronger; anticipated_direction is the expected raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast before evidence. For SMARCA2, SMARCA4 loss is tested within low- and high-aneuploidy strata to determine whether the very strong accepted effect spans aneuploidy status. For WRN, MSI-high status is tested in high- and low-hypoxia strata. For NFE2L2, KEAP1 loss is tested in STK11-loss cells and in high mutation-burden cells to examine pathway co-alteration and mutation-burden context. For USP7, TP53 loss is tested in high- and low-mutation-burden strata. For STAT3, PTEN loss is tested in high mutation burden and in low hypoxia as a complement to the accepted high-hypoxia result. For MDM2, CDKN2A loss is tested among TP53-intact cells with STK11 or KEAP1 co-alteration to refine the accepted CDKN2A-MDM2 axis into co-altered molecular contexts. These are associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal claims or claims of external generalizability. In later appraisal, results should be accepted only when the signed 95% interval excludes zero and the lower bound is large relative to the approximate 10% practical benchmark; near-null or zero-crossing results should be deferred or closed rather than repeatedly explored.",
