ather than accepted. H224 tests CDKN2A loss in TP53-intact KEAP1-loss lines and is not supported: signed +0.077 [-0.009,0.162], interval crosses zero and exposed cell is small. The upper bound leaves a clinically relevant effect possible, so I avoid a precise null and keep it unresolved/deferred. These accepted findings are associations within this supplied dataset only, not causal claims or externally generalizable claims; co-alteration structure and unmodeled technical factors could influence contexts, but the accepted effects are very large and pre-planned as localizations of already supported axes. No validation request is made because no new validation budget remains.",
