  "narrative": "I assessed the due validation response for H165. In the supplied dataset, MSI-high lines showed a very large and clinically meaningful stronger-dependency association for WRN within the high-aneuploidy stratum: the independent validation estimate is signed +0.778 in the registered stronger-dependency direction, with an adjusted 95% interval [0.708, 0.848]. This is consistent with the discovery estimate signed +0.801 [0.761, 0.841]. Even the lower bound is far above a conservative practical benchmark for these dependency scores, so H165 remains accepted and closed. The MSI-high/WRN axis therefore persists not only overall and in adenocarcinoma/adherent/Avana contexts, but also across low- and high-aneuploidy and low- and high-hypoxia strata tested so far. This is a dataset-specific association, not a causal claim or an external generalization.\n\nI also reassessed H205 as part of final synthesis. BRCA2 loss was associated only weakly with stronger POLR2A dependency in TP53-intact lines at discovery (signed +0.030 [-0.006, 0.066]), and independent validation was near null (signed +0.004 [-0.061, 0.069]). The combined evidence does not support a scientifically meaningful BRCA2-loss-associated POLR2A dependency effect in TP53-intact lines, so I reject and close H205 rather than continue treating it as a priority unresolved axis.\n\nThe strongest supported supplied-dataset dependency axes are: (1) SMARCA4 loss is associated with very strong SMARCA2 dependency, replicated with validation and stable across adenocarcinoma, ARID1A-intact, library, medium, stress-score, and aneuploidy contexts; (2) MSI-high is associated with very strong WRN dependency, replicated with validation and stable across lineage, culture, library, hypoxia, and aneuploidy contexts; (3) KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, replicated with validation and stable across TP53, STK11, MTAP, library, hypoxia, mutation-burden, and other molecular contexts; (4) CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, replicated with validation and robust in TP53-intact and TP53-loss settings, though co-altered STK11-loss and KEAP1-loss refinements remain uncertain; (5) TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency, replicated with validation and present in both high- and low-mutation-burden strata, MTAP-intact and CDKN2A contexts; and (6) PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency, replicated with validation and preserved across TP53 states, adenocarcinoma, PIK3CA, EMT, hypoxia, and mutation-burden contexts.\n\nThe main negative or unsupported findings are also clear. Matched driver-gene dependency hypotheses were largely not supported: KRAS mutation did not establish stronger KRAS dependency; BRAF V600E was not meaningfully associated with BRAF dependency; EGFR amplification did not robustly support stronger EGFR dependency; and ERBB2 amplification did not support stronger ERBB2 dependency in overall or refined contexts. MYC amplification and MYC-expression contexts did not support DHX9, POLR2A, RPL11, TMED10, or USP7 dependency. RB1 loss was not supported as a strong KIF18A dependency predictor, CDKN2A loss was not associated with stronger KRAS or KIF18A dependency overall, and the constructed research markers D/E/F behaved as null panels. BRCA2 loss was not a meaningful WRN predictor among MSI-negative lines and is now rejected for TP53-intact POLR2A dependency.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty remains mainly in interaction/context modification of the major axes, not in the main effects themselves. The TP53-loss-by-CDKN2A-loss interaction for USP7 remains unresolved because validation was wide and imprecise. MTAP-loss context for TP53-loss USP7, MTAP-related MDM2/CDKN2A interactions, PTEN-by-TP53 or adenocarcinoma localization of STAT3 dependency, and several borderline MDM2 co-alteration contexts remain unresolved. The most informative next analyses are not broad scans but these existing targeted follow-ups: CDKN2A loss effect on MDM2 dependency in TP53-intact MTAP-loss lines (H129), TP53-loss USP7 dependency in MTAP-loss lines and MTAP-loss interaction hypotheses (H182/H210), PTEN-loss STAT3 interactions and TP53/adenocarcinoma localizations (H154/H159/H208/H209), and limited MDM2 co-loss context refinement (H223/H224). No validation budget remains, so further work should be discovery-based and tightly targeted to these axes.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 final synthesis: H165 accepted/closed: MSI-high associated with very strong WRN dependency in high aneuploidy stratum, discovery signed +0.801 [0.761,0.841], validation signed +0.778 [0.708,0.848]. H205 rejected/closed: BRCA2-loss stronger POLR2A dependency in TP53-intact lines not supported after near-null validation (discovery +0.030 [-0.006,0.066]; validation +0.004 [-0.061,0.069]). Supported dataset axes: SMARCA4 loss -> very strong SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high -> very strong WRN dependency; KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency; CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency; PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency. These effects are replicated/robust across many molecular, lineage, library, culture, stress, and mutation-burden contexts. Negative/unsupported: matched driver dependency for KRAS/BRAF/EGFR/ERBB2, MYC-amplification contexts for DHX9/POLR2A/RPL11/TMED10/USP7, RB1 loss for KIF18A, CDKN2A for KRAS/KIF18A, research markers D/E/F, BRCA2 for WRN in MSI-negative and now TP53-intact POLR2A. Unresolved: MTAP-loss TP53/USP7, CDKN2A/MTAP MDM2 interactions, PTEN/STAT3 TP53/adenocarcinoma localizations, some MDM2 co-loss contexts, TP53 x CDKN2A USP7 interaction remains imprecise. No validation requests remain. Next analyses should be targeted to H129, H182/H210, H154/H159, H208/H209, and borderline MDM2 co-loss contexts only, not broad near-null scanning."
